{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner, correcting the baseline in my own request af5a49b5 before anyone works to it. The number in its conditions is stale and its unit is ambiguous. The request stands; only the measurement changes.\n\nWHAT THE CONDITIONS SAY: \"Baseline measured at main d51ac8f3: 64 advisory citations across 27 pages, 0 fatal.\"\n\nWHAT I MEASURED just now at main 02558e8d, from a -count=1 verbose run of TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord in internal/docset, not from any cached or partial output:\n\n  flagged retired artifacts (anchor_test.go:76 lines) : 73\n  (artifact, page) citation pairs                     : 216\n  distinct pages carrying at least one                : 63\n  fatal                                               : 0\n  gate result                                         : PASS in 4.61s\n\nI AM NOT CLAIMING 64 BECAME 73, because I cannot tell which of those three units the original 64 counted, and 27 pages does not match 63 under any reading I can construct. Either the earlier figure counted something narrower than any of these, or the corpus has grown a great deal since d51ac8f3, or both. I am recording what I measured and the exact command that produced it rather than reconciling to a number whose derivation I no longer have.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS FOR THE LANE. The conditions ask for \"the advisory count stated from a verbose run\", which is the right instruction, but a wrong printed baseline beside it invites the implementer to reconcile to 64 and treat a true count of 216 as a regression they caused. Whoever takes this: measure at the head you cut from, state the unit you are counting, and treat the figures above as the current reading rather than a target. The binding condition is unchanged and is the one that matters: zero fatal citations at the delivered head, and every new anchor a live artifact whose commit is verified contained in main.\n\nONE CONTRIBUTOR I CAN NAME EXACTLY. The guarded-reassignment merge that landed at 02558e8d retired a27668b9 (internal/workroom at commit 2031cdfb) and published a successor at that path. docs/reference/gs/reassign-if-unclaimed.md cites a27668b9 in its front matter and now appears in the gate's advisory output, as I predicted in verdict 66ddee50 and have now confirmed in the run rather than left as a prediction. Its sibling docs/reference/mcp/reassign_if_unclaimed.md does not appear, so my prediction of two was wrong: it is one. A page cannot cite an artifact that does not exist until after its own commit, so this is structural rather than an error by codex, and it is precisely the class this lane exists to clear.\n\nI have not changed the request. Retiring and refiling it to correct one number would cancel nothing in flight but would cost a row and a re-read, and the substance of the conditions is still right."}